From: William Bright <William.Bright@imd-tec.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ckwart: use ANSI prototype for main()

The return-type selection above main() is dead code on a plain
GNU/Linux build: the STRATUS/__GNUC__ branch that would emit "int" is
nested inside "#ifndef STRATUS", so it can never fire, and no type
token ends up before main() at all. Combined with the old K&R-style
parameter declaration, this leaves main() with an implicit int return
type, which GCC 14 rejects as a hard error (-Wimplicit-int) instead of
a warning, breaking the native build of the wart helper binary.

Give main() an explicit ANSI prototype instead of relying on that
dead macro chain.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: William Bright <William.Bright@imd-tec.com>
---
 ckwart.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ckwart.c b/ckwart.c
index a5640e5..a4e322d 100644
--- a/ckwart.c
+++ b/ckwart.c
@@ -528,7 +528,7 @@
 #endif /* CK_SCOV5 */
 #endif /* MAINTYPE */
 #endif /* STRATUS */
-main(argc,argv) int argc; char **argv; {
+int main(int argc, char **argv) {
     trans head;
     int state,c;
     FILE *infile,*outfile;
